{"id":"u-59c40d6c-074d-42d2-b8c0-18ce5c106b68","src":"community","title":"Reforged","author":"Michael S.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/UkQPvK-untitled-program","desc":"Reforged is an 8-week strength program designed for experienced lifters returning to training after an extended break. Rather than rushing back to previous workloads, Reforged systematically rebuilds strength, training volume, and work capacity through controlled progressive overload.\n\nThe program centers on the major compound lifts, beginning with moderate intensity and deliberately reduced volume. Each three-week training phase progressively adds repetitions while keeping the number of working sets and intensity stable, followed by a mandatory deload every fourth week to dissipate accumulated fatigue. The second training phase repeats the progression at a higher intensity.\n\nAccessory work provides additional hypertrophy and muscular development without overwhelming recovery, progressing alongside the primary lifts.\n\nReforged isn’t a beginner program. It’s a structured path back for lifters who already built strength—and are ready to build it again.\n\nPROGRAM INSTRUCTIONS\n\nFor the primary compound lifts, perform five working sets and progress by adding one repetition per set each week:\n\nWeek 1: 5 × 3\nWeek 2: 5 × 4\nWeek 3: 5 × 5\nRest 2-3 minutes between compound sets\n\nDeadlifts use three working sets instead:\n\nWeek 1: 3 × 3\nWeek 2: 3 × 4\nWeek 3: 3 × 5\nRest 1-2 minutes between accessory sets. \n\nFor accessory exercises, begin with two working sets in Week 1. Increase to three sets in Week 2. In Week 3, maintain three sets while slightly increasing the load.\n\nWeeks 4 and 8 are mandatory deloads. Reduce overall training volume by approximately 60% during these weeks to allow accumulated fatigue to dissipate before beginning the next training phase.\n\nRecommended: Minimum 20 minute treadmill walk/jog. Keep intensity low- Heart rate zone 1 to low zone 2 at maximum.","leve